+# TASK-051 round 2: records-migrate.py, the reviewers' findings on round 1 fixed (R-062)
+
+## Objective
+Fix the following confirmed defect — repair the named cause, nothing else. This round holds sixteen of them, F1 to F16 under Requirements, each a confirmed defect of round 1's `bridge/cursor-bridge/records-migrate.py` with its own named cause; the sentence above holds for each one separately.
+
+The program (round 1, already in the repository) is the migration of release B2: given a project root or record paths, it finds the eight record kinds' records and, for each record with no YAML front-matter header, writes one composed from `bridge_env`'s own fallback reading of the record's prose, atomically, read back before the move; with `--check` it writes nothing and lists what it would do. Round 1's reviewers found sixteen defects to fix now (F1 to F16). **The root cause, in one sentence, for every finding: a missing branch or a wrong condition at the cited line of round 1's program**; each finding's cause is proven by the code line it cites and by its reproduction test, which fails on round 1's program today (no diagnosis round is needed). The reproduction tests are committed in `tests/test_records_migrate.py`, in the section headed `# ---------------------------------------------------------------- round 2: the reviewers' findings on round 1`, above the builder's marker line: on round 1's program 17 of its 18 cases fail and 1 is skipped (the symbolic-link case, where the account cannot create a link). Each must go from red to green, the case that skips excepted where it still skips. Every case that passes today must still pass.
+
+Satisfies: R-062 - Migration is a program: `records-migrate.py` enumerates the eight kinds' records from a project root or from given paths and writes each header-less record's header from `bridge_env`'s fallback reading of its prose, atomically and read back before the move, marks `historic` from the one merged set, leaves a headed record unchanged, refuses a malformed one, lists what it cannot read or write, and with `--check` writes nothing. (Full text: the requirement's row in `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`. Its template and calibration half is TASK-052's, not yours.)
+
+## Scope
+Files and directories you may create or modify:
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/records-migrate.py
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/MANIFEST.json
+- docs/cli-reference.json
+- docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md
+- tests/test_records_migrate.py
+- docs/BUILDER_NOTES.md
+- handoff/TASK-051-r2-report.md
+
+Limits on these files:
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/records-migrate.py`: the fixes of F1 to F16 and nothing else.
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/MANIFEST.json` changes only as regenerated by `python tools/make-manifest.py` (Done, step 2). Never edit it by hand.
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/VERSION` is outside your Scope. `make-manifest.py` rewrites its line endings; leave the file as the command leaves it, edit it in no other way, and say in the report whether `git status --short` lists it. The supervisor restores it after your run.
+- `docs/cli-reference.json` and `docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md` change only if the program's command line changes, which this round should not do (no argument, option, default or help text is added, removed or renamed). Then, and only then, regenerate both with `python tools/dump-cli.py` and say in the report why the command line changed. Never edit either by hand.
+- `tests/test_records_migrate.py` is the supervisor's above its marker line, which reads exactly `# ---------------------------------------------------------------- builder's cases below this line`. Edit nothing above that line, the round-2 section and the module docstring included. Your own cases, round 1's and any you add now, live below it; round 1's cases below the marker stay and stay green.
+
+Do not modify anything else.
+
+## Out of scope
+- .env and anything under secrets/
+- CI configuration
+- docs/ and handoff/, except the files the Scope section names. Every record under docs/ is the supervisor's, `docs/diagrams/D-002-components.md` among them.
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge_env.py`, every other program under `bridge/cursor-bridge/`, `bridge/cursor-bridge/settings.bridge.json`, `tools/dump-cli.py` and `tools/make-manifest.py`. Call `bridge_env`'s functions; change none. If a fix seems to need a change there, stop and report it.
+- F17, not taken in this round: the program uses private `bridge_env` names (`_derived_historic`, `_PLAIN_WORD_RE`, `_PLAIN_TYPED_WORDS`, and others such as `_kind_norm`, `_plan_field_value`, `_demonstration_present`, `_REQ_STATUSES`). It is recorded for a later increment (to `docs/HARDENING.md`, by the supervisor). Leave those uses as they are and leave `bridge_env.py` untouched; do not replace them with copies of their logic.
+- `tests/test_dump_cli.py`, `tests/test_allowlist.py` and every test file other than `tests/test_records_migrate.py` (round 1 finished its changes to the first two).
+- Writing a header into any record of this repository (TASK-054). The templates and the calibration step (TASK-052).
+- Any mutation script. The mutants file and the mutation run are the supervisor's, after your run; this brief asks for the code fix only.
+
+## Context
+**The design that binds this program.** `docs/DESIGN.md`, section "## Change: release B2 (2026-11-04)": the paragraph beginning `**Writing.**` (the migration's design), "The reader" (the YAML subset the migration writes, and what it refuses) and "Header first; fallback; malformed". TASK-051's entry in `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md`.
+
+**The program as round 1 left it** (`bridge/cursor-bridge/records-migrate.py`, 675 lines; the line numbers below are this file's as committed). `_needs_quote(s)` 42-63 (the plain-or-quoted decision); `record_kind(rel)` 193-219 (the kind rule); `enumerate_records(root)` 222-244; `_plan_unbalanced_id(text)` 261-272 and `_plan_needs_merged(text)` 247-258; `compose_header(kind, text, rel, merged)` 414-439; `_status_cap_text(new_file)` 463-465; `_validate_read_back(kind, new_bytes, text, rel, merged)` 468-480; `_write_record(...)` 483-547 (the cap, the `--check` in-memory check, the temporary file, the read-back, `os.replace`); `_handle_headed(path, shown, kind, raw, check_mode)` 550-564; `main(argv)` 567-667.
